      "message": "pynfs has tests (LOOK3, OPEN10, CR9, CR9a, RNM6, RNM7, RM4, LINK6, SEC5) that expect NFS4ERR_INVAL for zero-length names, as the RFC requires. So file names (component4) and symlink text (linktext4) are allowed to be empty during decode, and the operations still return NFS4ERR_INVAL. The other utf8strings are rejected when empty.",
